**Day 28: Mini Project – Library DB (MySQL)**  

**Topic:**  
Design and implement a fully normalized Library Database (Library DB) using MySQL. Apply ER modeling, normalization techniques, and SQL skills to create a functional system for managing books, members, issues, and returns.  

**Learning Objectives:**  
• Design an Entity-Relationship (ER) model for a library management system.  
• Apply normalization (1NF, 2NF, 3NF) to eliminate data redundancy.  
• Implement SQL queries for CRUD operations on library data.  
• Integrate MySQL Workbench and Draw.io for database design and visualization.  

**Activities / Deliverables:**  
• Create an ER diagram using Draw.io to represent library entities and relationships.  
• Build a normalized MySQL database schema (tables for books, members, issues, returns).  
• Write SQL scripts for table creation, data insertion, and querying (e.g., book availability, member dues).  
• Demonstrate functional queries for issuing/returning books and generating reports.  

**Important Concepts:**  
• **ER Modeling:** Identifying entities (Book, Member, Issue, Return) and relationships (e.g., a member issues multiple books).  
• **Normalization:** Ensuring tables adhere to 3NF to avoid update anomalies.  
• **Referential Integrity:** Using foreign keys to enforce relationships (e.g., `issue.book_id` references `book.id`).  

**SQL Syntax / Commands:**  
• `CREATE TABLE` with constraints (PRIMARY KEY, FOREIGN KEY).  
• `INSERT INTO` to populate tables with sample data.  
• `SELECT` with JOINs to retrieve related data (e.g., books issued by a member).  
• `UPDATE`/`DELETE` with WHERE clauses for managing records.  

**Real-world Use Cases:**  
• Tracking book inventory and member borrowing history in libraries.  
• Automating overdue fine calculations and generating reports for librarians.  

**Tools / Tech:**  
• MySQL 8 (RDBMS for database creation and querying).  
• MySQL Workbench (schema design and SQL execution).  
• Draw.io (ER diagram visualization).  

**Summary:**  
Applied end-to-end database development skills by designing a normalized Library DB. Combined ER modeling, normalization, and SQL to build a functional system for managing library operations. Used MySQL Workbench and Draw.io for implementation and documentation.  

